package json

// The JSON surface of the `json` module (cppsrc/modules/json): `value.toJson()` is the value's
// JSON text, generated by the module's source generator beside this file
// (`generators/JsonGen.kt`), which the compiler carries built in.
//
// The declaration is what a call binds to and emits no C++ of its own - the generator emits one
// `toJson` extension per type the program uses, so a call reaches `toJson` by the receiver's own
// type (the shape `toString` has), and the generated extensions carry this name.
//
// The method is an extension rather than a free `toJson<T>(value: *T): Str` because a plain-name
// call is resolved by name and arity alone: a set of `toJson(*T)` overloads cannot be typed at a
// call site, while a member call is resolved by the receiver's type.
@SmGen("json")
fun T.toJson<T>(): Str
